s unfold as environmental puzzles in which rooms, props, memories, and staged scenes must be transformed to open a path forward.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >House of Tides has no traditional combat focus. Horror develops through disorientation, psychological pressure, sensory dissonance, unstable environments, and the gradual collapse between fiction and reality.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4865600/extras/a0ab3ebc5a190cec6b339e1eafde4231.poster.avif?t=1786981181\" width=1170 height=616 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4865600/extras/a0ab3ebc5a190cec6b339e1eafde4231.webm?t=1786981181\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4865600/extras/a0ab3ebc5a190cec6b339e1eafde4231.mp4?t=1786981181\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>A LABYRINTH OF MEMORIES AND IMAGINED LIVES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The theatre reaches beyond its physical rooms. Plays, memories, imagined lives, damaged archives, and fractured identities become spaces you can enter.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A museum, a home, an unfamiliar landscape, or an impossible stage may appear to be a separate reality while remaining part of the same theatrical system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Places return changed. Performances absorb details from other lives. Identities shift between person, character, memory, and invention.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https:/