erson psychological sci-fi horror set inside a forgotten theatre beneath a drowned world.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore a shifting labyrinth of memories, imagined lives, damaged archives, and fractured identities.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Investigate environments through objects, documents, recordings, theatrical fragments, and diegetic systems.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Use a technological bracelet to connect with the theatre and move between different spaces.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Progress through observation, visual alignment, sound, and environmental transformation.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Solve environmental puzzles shaped by the theatre’s history and the emotional logic of its scenes.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Follow voices, echoes, music, silence, distortions, and distant signals as narrative and mechanical clues.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Experience a story about grief, guilt, obsession, isolation, and the fragile need to connect with others.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A focused 3–5 hour single-player experience with no traditional combat focus.</p></li></ul>", "short_description": "Descend into a shifting labyrinth of memories, imagined lives, and fractured identities in this first-person psychological sci-fi horror game about grief, guilt, and obsession, set inside a forgotten theatre beneath a drowned world.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, Spanish - Spain<strong>*</strong>, Japanese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4865600/4fb25ecd7c160894c416887a2ccd6b29025465d1/header.jpg?t=1786981181", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4865600/3f1ae9bf09af70246ad203c3f80bb4cf3aa3926a/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1786981181", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_